        "title": "Text 1",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><strong>Sparrows and Explaining Your Ideas</strong></p><p>When working on a math problem, it is important to show how you solved the problem and explain your thinking. Adding text can help, but showing connections with arrows between mathematical objects to explain the connection can be a huge help. </p><p>Sparrows have many uses. They come in two forms.</p><ul><li>Curved, two-ended Sparrows</li><li>Straight, one-ended Sparrows</li></ul><p>Sparrows connect mathematical objects. This includes points, lines, shapes on any graphs or cells in a table. </p>"
          ]
        }
